# Copy to .env.local for local development, or set in your host's dashboard for deploys.
#
# Base URL of the Dhruv API. Leave EMPTY for local development so requests go to the Vite
# dev server, which proxies /api and /ws to localhost:8080 — that keeps the browser on a
# single origin, so the session cookie works with SameSite=Lax and no CORS is involved.
#
# In production set the full origin of the deployed API, e.g.
#   VITE_BACKEND_URL=https://api.dhruv.example.com
#
# Prefer a subdomain of the same registrable domain as the frontend (app.dhruv.example.com
# + api.dhruv.example.com). Same-site means the session cookie can stay SameSite=Lax.
# Splitting across unrelated domains (vercel.app + onrender.com) forces SameSite=None,
# which requires HTTPS and gives up SameSite as a CSRF defence layer.
VITE_BACKEND_URL=
